  "label": "The text 'they are the biggest terrorists in the history of the world' is mapped onto the group of people (including David Cameron) in the image.",
  "description": "The top text overlay makes an inflammatory and hateful claim about 'they' (implied to be Muslims or people of Muslim faith) being the biggest terrorists. This claim is analogically mapped onto the visual material, which depicts David Cameron and his supporters in a celebratory political rally. The juxtaposition implies that the group being vilified (Muslims) is being represented by the political figure and his supporters, even though the text is a gross generalization. The celebratory scene is contrasted with the hateful text, creating a mapping where the visual group is the target of the textual accusation.",
